<title>FINLAND: Clinton says NATO enlargement to go ahead on time.</title>
<headline>Clinton says NATO enlargement to go ahead on time.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. President Bill Clinton vowed on Friday that NATO enlargement would go ahead on schedule, despite Russian objections, and that the alliance would invite some Eastern European states to start membership talks at a Madrid summit in July.</p>
<p>&quot;I reaffirm that NATO enlargement at the Madrid summit will proceed,&quot; Clinton said after a summit with Russian President Boris Yeltsin. &quot;And President Yeltsin made it clear that he thinks it's a mistake,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
